{"seq":15,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:33:13.196Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"5be39cdd556e60bbae71b59c74fc227a8d1d80c9d52b51b3b7c8ee1ab5cb6cad","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"Bettina, here's what I found for Kwame's review (sources: #coastal-team, #coastal-random, Moss's Coastal digests, plus your Pellucid cutover note since it's public):\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics (Gulf Coast)\n- Ticket #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open. (Moss's Coastal cheat sheet)\n- Ticket #PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B (night dispatcher Hector, Beaumont). From your 2025-12-08 cutover recap, so it's old and I can't see its current status.\n- Not ticketed: a CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map, mentioned in the same recap with no number.\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight (Puget Sound)\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, asked for by their warehouse managers. (Coastal cheat sheet)\n- Ticket #4419: Moss's 2025-11-02 digest lists this number against DMF as a barge slip 7 schedule sync, with a patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift.\n- Not ticketed: Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B, which engineering worked around with a manual CSV patch (cheat sheet).\n\nCheck before the review: #4419 appears under both accounts, with different descriptions. Moss's two notes conflict, so one of them has the wrong number or account. Kwame should confirm which it is.\n\nLeft out: Pellow Home Living (PD-4821, #8812). I also left out Saltmarsh's PD-4824 and PD-4827, which aren't part of your request.\n\nThe Coastal channels have no other PHL or DMF ticket numbers, and I couldn't see any account ticket folders, so this list may not be complete.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok